      "id": "md2025_2293",
      "subset": "S5",
      "task_type": "cross-company-year-hybrid",
      "question": "Calculate the percentage increase in NFLX's total revenues from FY2022 to FY2024 and the percentage increase in paid memberships over the same period. How do these growth rates compare, and what does META's FY2022 and FY2024 MD&A provide for user or revenue metrics?",
      "expected_answer": "NFLX total revenues grew from $31,615,550 thousand in FY2022 to $39,000,966 thousand in FY2024, a 23.4% increase ($39,000,966 - $31,615,550) / $31,615,550 * 100 = 23.35%). Paid memberships at end of period grew from 230,747 thousand to 301,626 thousand, a 30.7% increase (($301,626 - $230,747) / $230,747 * 100 = 30.73%). Revenue grew slower than membership base, indicating ARPU pressure or mix shift. META's Item 7 for both FY2022 and FY2024 provides only introductory text with forward-looking statements, no revenue or user metrics, so no comparable data exists in the provided documents.",
      "predicted_answer": "NFLX total revenues rose 23.4% from FY2022 ($31,615,550 thousand) to FY2024 ($39,000,966 thousand), while paid memberships increased 30.7%, from 230,747 thousand to 301,626 thousand [C1][C2][E2][E3]. Membership growth therefore outpaced revenue growth over the period.\n\nMETA FY2022 Item 7: total revenue was $116.61 billion, down 1% versus 2021, reflecting a $5.96 billion negative FX impact; constant-currency revenue was $122.57 billion, up 4% [E4]. META FY2024 Item 7 supplies comparative income-statement data: revenue of $164,501 million in 2024, $134,902 million in 2023, and $116,609 million in 2022, but no user metrics in the supplied excerpt [E5][F5][F6].\n\nSources:\n[E2] NFLX_2024.html — Management's Discussion and Analysis of Financial Condition and Results of Operations\n[E3] NFLX_2022.html — Management's Discussion and Analysis of Financial Condition and Results of Operations\n[E4] META_2022.html — Item 7. Management's Discussion and Analysis of Financial Condition and Results of Operations\n[E5] META_2024.html — Item 7. Management's Discussion and Analysis of Financial Condition and Results of Operations",
